=== NON-SYMMETRIC strict-h0 K=4 VERY HETEROGENEOUS fixed-point study ===
Grid: G_inner=9, pad=2, UMAX_inner=4.0, G_full=13, du=1.0; FULL 4D inner block = 6561 unknowns (no multiset reduction).
Operator: phi_K4_halo (Numba, per-agent vectors), strict h=0, contour evidence = 3-axis-projection average over 3-other-agents level set.
NUMBA_NUM_THREADS=2.

[MILESTONE 1] HET CYTHON VALIDATION
  primary tau=[0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0] gamma=[0.05,0.25,1.0,4.0]:
    init_nl_match=0.00e+00 phi_nl_match=0.00e+00 phi_rand_match=0.00e+00 worst=0.00e+00 -> PASS (<=1e-11)
  anti    tau=[0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0] gamma=[4.0,1.0,0.25,0.05]:
    init_nl_match=0.00e+00 phi_nl_match=0.00e+00 phi_rand_match=0.00e+00 worst=0.00e+00 -> PASS (<=1e-11)
  Cython port is BIT-EXACT vs Numba with heterogeneous tau/gamma. Using Numba (faster: ~1.3 s/eval @2 threads vs ~2.5 s/eval Cython single-thread) for the runs.

[MILESTONE 2] NK HUNT (primary, FULL 6561 block, 5 seeds: cold_nolearn, fr_het, rand_0/1/2)
  No seed reaches Finf<1e-2 (non-smooth contour-crossing floor recurs, exactly like homogeneous K=4).
  cold_nolearn : floor F=0.401  het_def=0.204 (PR)
  fr_het       : floor F=0.038  het_def=0.038 (mid/near-FR) -- starts at exact lam(sum tau_i u_i), deficit 1e-11, NK drifts it only to 0.038
  rand_0       : floor F=0.432  het_def=0.126 (PR)
  rand_1       : floor F=0.088  het_def=0.099 (PR)
  rand_2       : floor F=0.110  het_def=0.100 (PR)
  KEY: the FR-het seed keeps the LOWEST deficit (~0.04, near-FR); off-FR seeds stall at PR (0.10-0.20).
  Unlike homogeneous K=4 (where the exact-FR seed sat at Finf~5e-6, a genuine FP), the het exact-FR
  price has residual ~0.069 init / 0.038 floor -- het-FR is only an APPROXIMATE Phi fixed point.
  -> deeper FR probe (more NK iters + Picard from fr_het) needed to decide FR vs PR; see below.

[MILESTONE 3] UNDAMPED PICARD (40 iters), primary het config
  From NL IC: het_def 0.352 -> 0.0062 (essentially FR; min 0.0062), step residual 0.376 -> non-smooth floor ~0.027.
              period2_oscillation = FALSE (d(n,n-2) median 0.059 stays >= d(n,n-1) median 0.029 -- both wobble around the
              non-smooth floor; NOT a clean 2-cycle). converged_clean=False only because of the contour floor, NOT instability.
  From exact het-FR seed: het_def stays ~0.0056 (does NOT drift to PR), residual floor ~0.011, no oscillation
              -> the het-FR price lam(sum_i tau_i u_i) is an APPROXIMATE, STABLE attractor under Picard.

[VERDICT] Very-heterogeneous tau (10x) / gamma (80x) does NOT reintroduce the K=3 partial-revelation/oscillation structure.
  K=4 stays FULLY-REVEALING (Picard-from-NL deficit -> 0.006, ~FR) and STABLE (no period-2 osc), like homogeneous K=4
  (-> FR, deficit ~0, no osc) and UNLIKE homogeneous K=3 (unique PR eq deficit ~0.27, period-2 learning oscillation).
  Only K=3 feature that survives: the non-smooth residual floor (~0.01-0.03 here; homogeneous K=4 had ~0.015).
  Heterogeneity is absorbed by the precision-weighted sufficient statistic sum_i tau_i u_i, not turned into info loss/instability.
  Saved: P_picard_nl_last_primary.npy (FR limit from NL IC), P_picard_fr_last_primary.npy (FR-seed stationary state),
         fig_k4_het_primary.png (NK residuals, Picard period-2 diagnostic, deficit trajectories).

[MILESTONE 4 / robustness] ANTI-ALIGNED config tau=[0.5,1,2,5], gamma=[4.0,1.0,0.25,0.05]
  (best-informed agent tau=5 is the MOST risk-NEUTRAL gamma=0.05 -- opposite pairing to primary)
  NK: fr_het seed reaches deficit ~0.007 (near-FR, lowest); off-FR seeds stall at PR 0.06-0.09; no seed Finf<1e-2.
  Picard from NL IC: het_def 0.177 -> 0.0019 (FR), period2=FALSE, floor ~0.024.
  Picard from FR seed: het_def stays 0.0015 (FR), no oscillation.
  -> SAME verdict as primary. The FR/stable conclusion is robust to whether high precision pairs with high or low
     risk aversion. Heterogeneity does NOT reintroduce K=3 partial-revelation/oscillation in either pairing.
